course: dictionary
lesson: 15549
title: Supernatural
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Supernatural means coming from beyond the natural world. Ghosts, magic and spirits are supernatural because science cannot explain them. Look at the word parts: super means beyond, and natural means of nature. So supernatural means beyond nature.
explain: «The old house had supernatural powers.» The word powers and the spooky house tell you the powers are strange, not normal. Ask yourself: could science explain this? If not, it may be supernatural.
explain: Supernatural can also be a noun with the: «the supernatural» means all things of this kind, such as ghosts, spells and monsters. In stories it brings fear and wonder, but in science lessons we look for natural explanations and evidence instead.
fact: Supernatural means beyond the natural world, and cannot be explained by science.
fact: «Supernatural beings» are creatures such as ghosts, spirits and monsters.
fact: «The supernatural» means all things of this kind: ghosts, spells, monsters and spirits.
fact: In science, pupils look for natural explanations and evidence instead of supernatural ones.
fact: Super means beyond, and natural means of nature: together they make supernatural.
exercise: «The witch used supernatural powers to make the frog talk.» What does supernatural mean here? | Very tired after a long day | Loud and cheerful | *Beyond nature, not explained by science | Made of soft wood
exercise: «Scientists look for natural explanations, not supernatural ones.» Which word means the opposite of supernatural? | *Natural | Spooky | Ghostly | Magical
exercise: «The ghost floated past the sleeping cat.» Find and copy one word that names a supernatural being. | cat | sleeping | floated | *ghost
test: Ella thinks the knocking in the attic is supernatural, but it was only the pipes. Why might a scientist say it is not supernatural? | Because ghosts knock every night | Because it was too loud to be real | Because pipes are magic | *Because it has a natural cause that science can explain
test: Which word is a noun meaning all things like ghosts, spells and spirits? | *the supernatural | supernatural | nature | natural
exam: «The film was full of supernatural beings, but the scientist tested every clue and found a natural cause.» What does this suggest about supernatural? | It means all films are scary | It means the scientist was a ghost | It means the film was true | *It describes things science cannot explain, and this event had a natural explanation
